      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T21:22:55Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(2d): arc turns and their radius on Face, 2D Contour and Slot\n\nFace and 2D Contour get `blend_radius` beside their `blend_turns`.\nSlot gets `blend_turns` and `blend_radius`.\n\n- 2D Contour: the air-side corner arcs take the radius. No radius is the\n  tool radius, as before.\n- Face: a radius below half the row spacing turns each row end on two\n  quarter arcs with a straight step, one radius outside the overrun\n  line. No radius is the semicircle, as before. With a radius, rows\n  spaced wider than the tool diameter turn on arcs too.\n- Slot: each row-end corner of the serpentine turns on one tangent arc\n  inside the cutter-center stadium (new module `slot_turns`). The note\n  states the corner rest.\n\nThe parameter door refuses a radius below 0.01 mm. The generators refuse\na radius past the tool radius. The project file writes the keys only\nwhen set, and the digest reads the radius only when the option is on, so\na default operation keeps its path, its file and its stamp.\n\nFixes #1759\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
