      "message": "fix(2d): keep the Face corner arc at or below the requested radius\n\nA Face row turn whose half spacing exceeded the radius by less than\n0.005 mm took the semicircle, which is larger than the radius. Now it\ntakes corner arcs shrunk to keep the straight-step floor, or stays\nsharp (named Tiny refusal) when those would be below the arc resolution.\n\nPinned by blend::law::a_short_step_never_turns_on_an_arc_larger_than_the_radius\nand arc_turn_kinds::a_face_turn_never_exceeds_the_radius_when_the_straight_step_is_short.\n\nRefs #1759\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
